# Starts msime-client-clipboard.service at login for users who enabled it, on sessions without graphical-session.target (Sway, i3, Hyprland without uwsm), where the unit's WantedBy never fires; this is how the clipboard monitor starts with the IME at every login as it does on Windows. Where that target is active it already started the service and this does nothing, and a user who never enabled the service is left alone. Otherwise it hands this session's display to the user manager and restarts the service, so an instance left over from an earlier session (lingering user manager) follows the new display.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=MSIME Clipboard
Name[zh_CN]=水杉输入法剪贴板历史
Exec=sh -c "systemctl --user -q is-enabled msime-client-clipboard.service || exit 0; systemctl --user -q is-active graphical-session.target && exit 0; systemctl --user import-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY DISPLAY XAUTHORITY; exec systemctl --user restart msime-client-clipboard.service"
NoDisplay=true
Terminal=false
